n; but the state cannot have both. Usually they wouldn't include both. I suspect the init is meant to have (vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma) and not have candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma; but they wrote it incorrectly. However we see also (candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma) in init. Let's check other vehicle links: (candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta) and (vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha) and (vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha) and (vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_alpha) and (vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma). So they intend vehicle_unit_gamma to be free, but also they linked shift_candidate_alpha to vehicle_unit_gamma maybe erroneously. Actually they might have meant that shift_candidate_alpha is linked to vehicle_unit_gamma? But then vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_alpha is true, so vehicle_unit_gamma should be allocated, thus not available. Yet they also say vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma. That is inconsistent. We need to decide which to trust. Since the goal includes (vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta) and (vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha) and (vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta). Also goal includes (candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma). So they want shift_candidate_beta to be linked to vehicle_unit_gamma, and vehicle_unit_gamma to be allocated (so not available). The goal also includes (vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha) and (vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta). So after plan, vehicle_unit_alpha and beta should be available (i.e., not allocated). Initially they are allocated to origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha respectively (and those are allocated). Goal wants them to be dispatched and then become available after dispatch (since dispatch action makes vehicle_available). So that matches: after dispatching origin and destination, their vehicles 